WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:09.092
[opening theme song playing]

00:45.086 --> 00:46.504
- [sloshing]
- [glass clinking]

00:46.588 --> 00:49.215
[gentle music]

00:58.433 --> 01:00.101
[Ha-kyung] Atmospheric instability

01:00.185 --> 01:03.521
is the collision of two types of air
with different properties.

01:04.272 --> 01:06.399
[sloshing]

01:12.864 --> 01:14.866
[dreamy music]

01:24.876 --> 01:26.920
[dreamy music continues]

01:31.966 --> 01:35.303
[birds chirping]

01:39.891 --> 01:42.143
[phone vibrates]

01:51.194 --> 01:52.821
[vibrating continues]

01:58.201 --> 01:59.285
[sighs]

02:02.872 --> 02:03.748
I'm late.
[gasps]

02:03.832 --> 02:04.916
[Si-woo groans]

02:06.167 --> 02:08.128
- [panting]
- [Si-woo moans]

02:08.920 --> 02:09.921
[slams]

02:10.672 --> 02:11.840
[groans]

02:16.553 --> 02:18.138
[moans]

02:18.221 --> 02:19.514
[panting]

02:20.014 --> 02:21.057
[Si-woo] I'm not ready yet.

02:21.558 --> 02:23.643
- Oh, no, we can't go in together.
- We're gonna be late, though.

02:23.726 --> 02:25.103
Not "we," just you.

02:25.186 --> 02:27.981
- [door opens]
- [door lock chimes]

02:28.731 --> 02:30.233
- [door closes]
- [chuckles]

02:33.027 --> 02:34.362
THE EFFECTIVENESS OF FOG ADVISORIES
AND CASES FROM ABROAD

02:36.948 --> 02:38.783
[phone vibrates]

02:43.580 --> 02:45.582
[unsettling music]

02:47.250 --> 02:49.419
[vibrating continues]

02:49.502 --> 02:50.545
[sighs]

02:57.886 --> 02:58.845
Hello?

03:03.850 --> 03:04.684
[inhales]

03:13.151 --> 03:14.986
[elevator dings]

03:16.154 --> 03:17.405
[hurried footsteps]

03:19.032 --> 03:20.033
[lock chiming]

03:22.368 --> 03:24.537
[switch clicks]

03:26.497 --> 03:27.874
So what do you want me to do?

03:28.917 --> 03:31.586
Listen. I won't do anything for you.

03:31.669 --> 03:33.546
Not anymore. And I can't anyway!

03:34.339 --> 03:35.632
And don't ever call me.

03:37.342 --> 03:38.426
[call ends]

03:39.177 --> 03:40.094
[exhales sharply]

03:42.096 --> 03:44.432
[mysterious music]

03:48.186 --> 03:52.690
[Ha-kyung] When cold air
suddenly meets hot air…

03:56.402 --> 03:58.071
I, uh, forgot my hard drive.

03:59.197 --> 04:00.114
Ah.

04:02.784 --> 04:04.160
I was gonna bring it for you.

04:07.872 --> 04:08.706
Well, thanks.

04:11.125 --> 04:13.127
So, um, who was that?

04:13.211 --> 04:15.088
[mysterious music continues]

04:17.173 --> 04:18.967
It's just someone that I used to know.

04:20.260 --> 04:21.135
Oh.

04:22.804 --> 04:26.724
…the atmosphere becomes unstable
and severe weather occurs.

04:29.018 --> 04:31.312
Shouldn't you go? You're gonna be late.

04:31.896 --> 04:33.398
Uh, yeah, I should.

04:35.275 --> 04:36.859
[door opens]

04:36.943 --> 04:38.278
Uh, I'll go along.

04:42.740 --> 04:44.867
[Yu-jin] Where are you going?
We need to talk.

04:44.951 --> 04:45.868
Later.

04:47.704 --> 04:48.746
[sighs]

04:51.416 --> 04:53.376
I didn't know you were someone
who holds a grudge.

04:53.960 --> 04:56.337
- What?
- [thuds]

04:56.421 --> 04:58.172
Do you think I'm holding
a grudge right now?

04:58.256 --> 05:00.216
Okay, so Lee Si-woo
and I went on some dates.

05:00.300 --> 05:02.802
I met him when I was working
at the Metro Office.

05:02.885 --> 05:04.554
He was nice,
and for a few months, we went out.

05:05.138 --> 05:06.889
So? Anything else you want to know?

05:07.473 --> 05:10.435
How about my college crushes,
my first love in high school?

05:10.518 --> 05:12.562
Why can't you see why I'm upset?

05:12.645 --> 05:15.315
You think this is just about a guy
you happened to date?

05:15.398 --> 05:16.399
Oh, it's not?

05:16.482 --> 05:17.734
You lied to me before.

05:17.817 --> 05:19.527
[Ki-jun] You said you never met him.

05:19.610 --> 05:21.237
I just don't get why you would lie.

05:21.821 --> 05:24.907
I didn't want things to be uncomfortable
since we all work together.

05:26.034 --> 05:27.702
Just like how uncomfortable I am

05:27.785 --> 05:29.787
seeing that woman
every time I go in there.

05:29.871 --> 05:32.540
I'm not okay with it
just because I don't say anything.

05:33.124 --> 05:35.626
I told you about her at the start.
I told you if I had--

05:35.710 --> 05:38.421
And you have always told me
that the past is the past, so…

05:40.381 --> 05:41.257
Ah.

05:42.425 --> 05:44.469
So you're saying
it was the past at our wedding

05:44.552 --> 05:46.262
when he made a whole scene over us?

05:49.557 --> 05:51.434
[sighs]
Forget it.

05:54.896 --> 05:56.397
Hey, we're not done talking.

05:56.981 --> 05:59.192
I'll be late if I stay here any longer.

05:59.275 --> 06:01.319
Plus, I have to clean up
your whole mess too.

06:02.612 --> 06:03.863
- [door lock beeps]
- [door opens]

06:05.156 --> 06:06.074
[door slams]

06:06.699 --> 06:07.700
[door lock chimes]

06:07.784 --> 06:08.701
[exhales sharply]

06:12.246 --> 06:14.040
- [phone vibrates]
- [sighs]

06:18.586 --> 06:20.338
[vibrating continues]

06:21.631 --> 06:22.507
[sighs]

06:23.466 --> 06:26.719
[reporter] Warmer weather right now
than we usually see in early June.

06:26.803 --> 06:30.098
Today will be a hot one
with temperatures rising sharply.

06:30.181 --> 06:34.018
Currently, 23 degrees in Seoul
and 21 in Incheon,

06:34.102 --> 06:36.187
down one or two degrees from yesterday.

06:36.270 --> 06:39.774
But midday temperatures
are expected to get as high as 29 degrees.

06:39.857 --> 06:41.818
Even though June is the start of summer,

06:41.901 --> 06:44.237
we won't see true summer heat
for a little while.

06:44.320 --> 06:46.364
Skies are looking clear all day.

06:46.447 --> 06:48.741
Cloudless skies mean strong
direct sun throughout the day,

06:48.825 --> 06:50.409
so be mindful of UV…

06:50.493 --> 06:52.662
You should drive with both your hands
on the wheel.

06:52.745 --> 06:55.081
[chuckles]
I'm good with just one, though.

06:56.415 --> 06:58.334
[chuckles]
Drive safely, though.

06:59.877 --> 07:00.920
Okay.

07:02.672 --> 07:04.549
[Ha-kyung] Two different mindsets.

07:05.716 --> 07:07.677
[phone vibrating]

07:08.177 --> 07:09.846
CHAE YU-JIN

07:12.348 --> 07:13.224
[vibrating continues]

07:15.143 --> 07:15.977
[Si-woo] Um…

07:16.060 --> 07:17.895
I have to drive safely right now.

07:18.479 --> 07:19.397
Right?

07:19.480 --> 07:20.523
[chuckles awkwardly]

07:22.150 --> 07:24.026
[Ha-kyung] Two different scars.

07:29.615 --> 07:34.662
KOREA METEOROLOGICAL ADMINISTRATION

07:38.791 --> 07:40.376
Drop me off in front of the crosswalk.

07:41.002 --> 07:42.336
Why? We're almost there.

07:42.420 --> 07:43.671
Why can't we just go?

07:43.754 --> 07:44.922
Drop me off.

07:45.006 --> 07:46.883
Jeez, just 'cause somebody could see us?

07:46.966 --> 07:48.801
I could just say I ran into you
coming over here.

07:48.885 --> 07:50.344
Should I just get out?

07:51.721 --> 07:55.433
[Ha-kyung] Just like when cold air
suddenly meets hot air,

07:55.516 --> 07:59.312
you and I, two different people, met.

08:01.355 --> 08:02.273
[sighs]

08:02.940 --> 08:03.858
All right.

08:04.484 --> 08:06.402
- I'll drop you off over there.
- [chuckles]

08:06.486 --> 08:08.321
You should get over right now.

08:09.572 --> 08:10.823
[yawns]

08:12.283 --> 08:13.242
Mm?

08:13.326 --> 08:15.077
[playful music]

08:15.161 --> 08:16.412
[Seok-ho] Uh…

08:17.955 --> 08:19.749
[chuckling awkwardly]

08:20.541 --> 08:21.709
[soft chuckle]

08:21.792 --> 08:23.961
[playful music continues]

08:26.380 --> 08:28.216
[Ha-kyung] We already committed to this.

08:29.592 --> 08:32.845
How much unstable climates
caused by this decision

08:33.554 --> 08:35.473
will we be able to avoid?

08:36.766 --> 08:43.022
EPISODE 5
LOCALIZED HEAVY RAIN

08:43.105 --> 08:45.107
[quirky music]

08:49.278 --> 08:50.613
[whispers]
Say something.

08:55.076 --> 08:57.036
- We met on our way here.
- Huh?

08:58.037 --> 09:00.790
It's just we, by total coincidence,
ran into each other.

09:01.749 --> 09:02.667
Uh-huh.

09:03.668 --> 09:04.919
[Ha-kyung] What a coincidence.

09:08.714 --> 09:11.217
[Seok-ho breathes deeply]

09:11.300 --> 09:13.844
Looks like traffic in Uijeongbu
has been backed up all morning

09:13.928 --> 09:15.263
'cause the roads are flooded.

09:15.346 --> 09:16.722
The Jungnang River overflowed.

09:17.431 --> 09:19.267
"Flooded"? The Jungnang River?

09:19.850 --> 09:21.811
It rained in Uijeongbu overnight.

09:21.894 --> 09:23.437
It was like 50mm per hour.

09:23.521 --> 09:24.772
[Ha-kyung and Si-woo in unison] Rain?

09:25.356 --> 09:27.650
[uneasy music]

09:27.733 --> 09:28.901
[Bong-chan] Mm.

09:29.735 --> 09:32.154
[sucks teeth]
Uh, I'm not, uh…

09:32.989 --> 09:35.283
Isn't it too early
for localized heavy rainfall like this?

09:35.366 --> 09:39.036
[Young-gil] In terms of development,
it's a pretty standard sudden downpour.

09:39.120 --> 09:40.871
It took exactly 21 minutes

09:40.955 --> 09:44.584
for Uijeongbu's rain
to travel to Namyangju.

09:44.667 --> 09:47.211
A heavy rain advisory
was issued around 5:30 a.m.

09:47.295 --> 09:50.256
Total predicted rainfall
is somewhere around 70 and 80mm.

09:50.339 --> 09:52.675
[Bong-chan] Where's
the precipitation concentrated?

09:52.758 --> 09:54.594
Near the Jungnang River footbridge.

09:54.677 --> 09:56.554
[Bong-chan sighs]
Jungnang River? My goodness.

09:56.637 --> 09:59.640
And I guess by the time the advisory
was out, it was already too late.

10:00.224 --> 10:01.809
- Yes.
- Oh!

10:02.685 --> 10:05.313
Director Jin. What do you think?

10:05.396 --> 10:08.399
Don't you think
the water vapor inflow is oddly high?

10:08.482 --> 10:10.985
Yesterday's daytime high
was around 30 degrees

10:11.068 --> 10:13.571
and provided a lot of ground heat
in that region.

10:13.654 --> 10:17.908
As a result, the atmosphere over there
is likely to create strong conditions.

10:17.992 --> 10:20.995
No, no, the biggest cause
looks like the instability

10:21.078 --> 10:22.622
just north of Uijeongbu.

10:22.705 --> 10:24.707
The air's, the air's extremely cold.

10:24.790 --> 10:27.043
Huh? Elaborate.

10:27.668 --> 10:30.129
Oh! So, if you look over here,
the temperature difference

10:30.212 --> 10:32.214
between the upper and lower layers
of the atmosphere

10:32.298 --> 10:34.300
near Uijeongbu is almost 40 degrees.

10:37.762 --> 10:38.638
[Bong-chan] Mm.

10:39.263 --> 10:40.264
- Director Jin.
- Yes?

10:40.848 --> 10:43.434
- Run an analysis for this.
- Yes, of course.

10:45.895 --> 10:48.272
How astute. Well done.

10:48.773 --> 10:50.149
I'm glad I brought you here
to Headquarters.

10:50.232 --> 10:52.068
- [chuckles]
- Thank you, sir.

10:53.152 --> 10:55.696
[Bong-chan sucks teeth]
All right, then.

10:56.197 --> 10:58.741
[cheeky music]

10:59.659 --> 11:01.619
[Soo-jin] Of all those rain echoes,

11:01.702 --> 11:04.664
how do you know which one
will develop into a sudden storm?

11:04.747 --> 11:05.915
With only an hour?

11:05.998 --> 11:06.957
[inhales]

11:07.041 --> 11:09.251
Let's say you started boiling water
on a stove.

11:09.835 --> 11:11.754
It's similar to guessing
the place in the pot

11:11.837 --> 11:14.048
where the bubbles
are going to start first.

11:14.131 --> 11:15.174
Huh?

11:15.257 --> 11:16.425
[chuckles]

11:16.509 --> 11:20.346
It's better not to try and predict
if you're trying not to go crazy.

11:21.013 --> 11:22.223
- [hand taps]
- [sighs]

11:23.849 --> 11:25.393
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

11:25.476 --> 11:27.520
All right, all right.
[clapping]

11:27.603 --> 11:29.230
Don't worry, huh?

11:29.814 --> 11:31.148
Think of it like a quick jab

11:31.232 --> 11:33.150
thrown from the sky
to keep us on our toes.

11:33.234 --> 11:34.151
All right?

11:34.860 --> 11:37.655
So let's all stay responsible, eyes open.

11:37.738 --> 11:38.656
Okay?

11:40.199 --> 11:42.618
Quick reporting of storms is vital.

11:43.536 --> 11:44.412
That is all.

11:44.495 --> 11:45.579
Good job, everyone.

11:45.663 --> 11:47.164
- [woman 1] Thank you, sir.
- [man 1] Thank you.

11:47.248 --> 11:48.165
[man 2] Thank you, sir.

11:48.249 --> 11:49.166
[woman 2] Thank you.

11:49.250 --> 11:50.835
[door opens]

11:50.918 --> 11:52.545
- [man 3] How you doing?
- What's up, man?

11:53.337 --> 11:55.005
I'm sorry, ma'am. I'm sorry I'm late.

11:56.924 --> 11:58.759
- Mr. Um.
- Yes?

12:02.763 --> 12:03.848
Let's talk over coffee.

12:05.182 --> 12:07.393
- [sighs]
- [Bong-chan] Come on.

12:07.476 --> 12:08.394
Yes, sir.

12:09.395 --> 12:10.354
[sighs]

12:12.898 --> 12:15.151
[doors slide open]

12:20.531 --> 12:23.534
[Dong-han] Oh. Mm… Thanks.

12:23.617 --> 12:24.618
[Dong-han chuckles]

12:24.702 --> 12:27.455
Didn't you go straight home
after we got that drink last night?

12:27.538 --> 12:31.959
Ah! I couldn't sleep,
so I thought I'd have one more, eh.

12:32.042 --> 12:34.753
- And one led to--
- Well, this is a new one.

12:34.837 --> 12:36.297
[Bong-chan] The great Um Dong-han

12:36.380 --> 12:39.467
showing up during monsoon season late
and with a hangover.

12:39.550 --> 12:40.593
[chuckles]

12:42.887 --> 12:45.139
- [can clanks]
- So what's going on?

12:46.348 --> 12:49.935
The sky changes, it's…
It's a new pattern every three days.

12:50.019 --> 12:52.062
Again, always stay the same.

12:53.689 --> 12:55.065
Something wrong at the house?

12:57.443 --> 12:58.694
[chuckles]
No, nothing's wrong.

13:02.031 --> 13:03.073
- [can thuds]
- [sighs]

13:04.575 --> 13:06.160
All you care about is weather.

13:06.744 --> 13:08.996
Any kind of weather,
you'll go sun, you'll go storms.

13:09.079 --> 13:12.875
You'll wander around the whole world
and maybe stop at home for a day.

13:12.958 --> 13:14.460
Then the next morning, you tell me

13:14.543 --> 13:16.837
you would have to leave again
for some stupid reason, right?

13:16.921 --> 13:18.714
[Hyang-rae] You were never there, ever.

13:19.298 --> 13:21.008
So we've tried to move on.

13:22.176 --> 13:23.928
We've made it 14 years without you.

13:24.720 --> 13:26.138
You understand me now?

13:28.641 --> 13:29.892
[apron rustles]

13:36.774 --> 13:38.859
[emotional music]

13:42.738 --> 13:43.781
[door closes]

13:47.326 --> 13:49.453
[luggage clanking]

13:54.124 --> 13:56.669
What's this? Going somewhere?

13:59.088 --> 14:00.256
Oh, um…

14:01.215 --> 14:03.133
I must stay at the office for a while.

14:04.552 --> 14:07.263
There's a lot of work to do
during the monsoon season.

14:08.347 --> 14:09.765
Do you really have to go?

14:10.432 --> 14:12.601
This way, everything's easier
for you and Bo-mi.

14:12.685 --> 14:13.936
Do what you want.

14:14.478 --> 14:16.522
If you're gonna be like this,
you should have stayed away.

14:19.108 --> 14:21.610
[emotional music]

14:22.236 --> 14:24.071
[water running]

14:27.533 --> 14:29.577
[emotional music continues]

14:33.122 --> 14:35.291
- [door lock beeps]
- [door opens]

14:38.586 --> 14:40.421
[slurping]

14:54.143 --> 14:57.479
[steam hisses]

14:59.273 --> 15:01.567
[Soo-jin] Does Senior Forecaster Um
drink a lot?

15:01.650 --> 15:04.570
- I don't know. Not that I've heard of.
- Hmm.

15:05.154 --> 15:08.782
Well, I guess it must be hard for him
'cause of his failed promotion.

15:08.866 --> 15:10.409
[gasps]
Don't you think? Hmm?

15:11.410 --> 15:12.286
Well, I think so.

15:13.162 --> 15:14.121
I don't know.

15:14.204 --> 15:15.873
Hello. Attention, everyone.

15:16.916 --> 15:17.917
We're going to analyze

15:18.000 --> 15:20.461
the flash flood-related signals
over the past ten years,

15:20.544 --> 15:23.589
including duration and levels
as well as sort it by region.

15:23.672 --> 15:24.840
Everything for ten years?

15:24.924 --> 15:25.841
Yes.

15:27.635 --> 15:29.929
Is ten years of reports really necessary?

15:30.512 --> 15:32.681
This morning was
an extremely unusual case.

15:32.765 --> 15:34.350
It was, but climate change

15:34.433 --> 15:37.227
could still be increasing
the overall likelihood of such phenomena.

15:37.311 --> 15:39.480
We need to think long-term about it, okay?

15:39.563 --> 15:41.315
There's a lot of uncertainty right now.

15:41.398 --> 15:44.610
I think a short-term analysis
would be more helpful

15:44.693 --> 15:47.029
in supporting our forecasting goals
at the current moment.

15:47.112 --> 15:50.074
The Director General also said
real-time monitoring is key.

15:50.157 --> 15:53.577
Isn't real-time monitoring
more valuable in this situation?

15:53.661 --> 15:56.121
[pensive music]

16:02.086 --> 16:04.380
[pensive music continues]

16:06.799 --> 16:09.343
Let's proceed with our ten years
of analysis, please.

16:12.554 --> 16:15.724
- Ugh, today really sucks.
- [mouse clicking]

16:21.230 --> 16:22.356
[sighs]

16:23.315 --> 16:24.191
[phone vibrates]

16:39.623 --> 16:41.750
[doors slide open]

16:43.293 --> 16:44.461
HOW ACCURATE IS THE RAIN FORECAST?

16:44.545 --> 16:46.755
- [woman 1] Did you check?
- [woman 2] I'll call them right now.

16:47.965 --> 16:49.008
[Ki-jun] What is this?

16:49.508 --> 16:51.468
Why are the article stories all different?

16:51.552 --> 16:54.430
We found out about the flood
after the advisory was issued.

16:54.513 --> 16:57.766
We put out the press release right away.
But some outlets had already printed.

16:58.642 --> 16:59.893
- [pen clacks]
- [sighs]

17:01.687 --> 17:04.898
- Which team is in charge right now?
- They probably changed shifts already.

17:05.899 --> 17:06.942
So it's Two right now.

17:07.026 --> 17:08.652
Our second team?

17:09.737 --> 17:11.947
[tense music]

17:12.698 --> 17:15.284
TREAT THE SKIES AS A FRIEND
AND THE PEOPLE AS THE SKIES

17:15.367 --> 17:17.286
"Chief Team Two."

17:18.954 --> 17:21.206
[whispering]
Chief Team Two. Chief Team Two.

17:21.290 --> 17:23.333
[upbeat music]

17:24.543 --> 17:27.421
Chief Team Two. Chief Team Two.

17:31.467 --> 17:32.968
FORECAST TRAINING

17:36.513 --> 17:38.557
[upbeat music continues]

17:43.020 --> 17:43.854
I got a call

17:44.646 --> 17:45.522
What call?

17:53.864 --> 17:54.698
[Yu-jin exhales]

17:54.782 --> 17:57.868
We're over now. How long
will I keep getting these calls?

17:57.951 --> 17:58.911
I'm sorry.

18:00.120 --> 18:01.497
You can block the number.

18:01.580 --> 18:03.916
I'm already in enough trouble
right now because of you.

18:03.999 --> 18:05.209
Because of me?

18:05.292 --> 18:06.627
Ki-jun found out the truth.

18:07.544 --> 18:08.796
He found out about us two.

18:08.879 --> 18:10.798
It's already done, so what's the problem?

18:10.881 --> 18:12.257
[groans]

18:12.341 --> 18:14.635
Why did you have to make a scene
at my wedding, though?

18:14.718 --> 18:18.806
Also, why did you have to transfer
to Headquarters right after my honeymoon?

18:19.890 --> 18:22.434
I can't blame Ki-jun
for thinking this is all strange.

18:23.310 --> 18:24.228
[exhales sharply]

18:25.437 --> 18:26.480
[heavy sigh]

18:26.563 --> 18:27.523
[Si-woo] So?

18:28.690 --> 18:29.733
You two fought?

18:31.652 --> 18:33.070
And now he's mad, huh?

18:33.904 --> 18:35.322
[scoffs]

18:35.405 --> 18:37.366
Ki-jun is not that kind of person.

18:37.991 --> 18:39.159
He's really in love with me.

18:40.035 --> 18:42.579
He wouldn't get bitter
over something that doesn't matter.

18:42.663 --> 18:43.539
[sighs]

18:44.164 --> 18:46.875
Okay. Well, I guess I'll be more careful.
That all you want?

18:46.959 --> 18:48.293
Of course. Of course, that's all.

18:50.420 --> 18:51.338
[gasps]

18:52.005 --> 18:53.340
[Yu-jin] Uh, oppa.

18:53.423 --> 18:55.592
[uneasy music]

18:59.972 --> 19:01.974
[uneasy music continues]

19:05.769 --> 19:06.937
What are you doing?

19:07.729 --> 19:08.772
We were just talking.

19:09.439 --> 19:10.482
You know…

19:11.692 --> 19:14.361
the Weather Team shouldn't ever talk
directly to the media.

19:15.320 --> 19:17.573
That's what
the Spokesperson's Office is for.

19:19.032 --> 19:23.287
This is why every newspaper in town
has different stories about the rain.

19:23.370 --> 19:25.873
Can I talk to you, oppa?
I can explain this.

19:25.956 --> 19:28.083
Stay out of this, reporter.
This is KMA business.

19:29.751 --> 19:31.795
Why are you like this, huh?

19:31.879 --> 19:34.298
I guess I don't know
'cause you just started at Headquarters.

19:34.381 --> 19:36.216
The Spokesperson's Office
is the voice of KMA.

19:36.300 --> 19:39.219
Even if your forecast is good,
if you don't work with the Spokesperson,

19:39.303 --> 19:41.054
the reports are going to be
all over the place

19:41.138 --> 19:42.431
like the flash flood release this morning.

19:43.015 --> 19:45.434
I know. If communication
between the Media Office

19:45.517 --> 19:47.728
and the reporters was going
smoothly in the first place,

19:47.811 --> 19:50.272
our forecast team wouldn't have
to get involved in this at all.

19:50.355 --> 19:52.441
How can you say that
when you hold things back, huh?

19:53.025 --> 19:55.527
Who said that you could
keep on crossing boundaries?

19:55.611 --> 19:58.197
You should know since you've been
at Headquarters for so long.

19:58.280 --> 20:00.407
Our forecast room is the KMA's heart.

20:01.491 --> 20:04.369
Do you know a heart that would ask
for your permission to beat?

20:05.037 --> 20:06.163
What?

20:06.246 --> 20:08.332
[tense music]

20:09.041 --> 20:11.627
If you really wanna stay enlightened
regarding our forecasts,

20:11.710 --> 20:12.961
come to the Situation Room,

20:13.045 --> 20:15.339
and you can watch
the way we handle things.

20:20.260 --> 20:21.178
[scoffs]

20:23.972 --> 20:24.890
[clicks tongue]

20:26.016 --> 20:28.143
[tense music continues]

20:31.480 --> 20:32.397
[sighs]

20:40.155 --> 20:41.990
[phone vibrates]

20:47.829 --> 20:49.581
[vibrating continues]

20:51.375 --> 20:52.459
[sighs]

20:55.837 --> 20:57.172
[Ki-jun] Who does he think he is?

20:57.756 --> 21:00.509
I mean, am I wrong to ask
for an immediate update

21:00.592 --> 21:03.095
for the Spokesperson's Office
on the severe weather conditions?

21:03.178 --> 21:06.265
Also, why does he think
he can talk in secret with a reporter?

21:06.348 --> 21:07.933
A reporter who's married too.

21:08.016 --> 21:09.393
The nerve of that punk.

21:10.352 --> 21:11.937
She's my wife.

21:12.020 --> 21:13.063
[scoffs]

21:13.146 --> 21:16.858
And worse, they were talking right here
on KMA grounds for everyone to see?

21:16.942 --> 21:17.859
You found out.

21:19.069 --> 21:19.945
What?

21:20.737 --> 21:22.990
Lee Si-woo is Chae Yu-jin's ex.

21:24.825 --> 21:27.411
- You knew about it?
- Mm-hmm.

21:27.494 --> 21:29.621
- For how long?
- Since he first came here.

21:29.705 --> 21:30.622
[scoffs]

21:31.373 --> 21:33.709
[Ki-jun] And you still let him on
to your team?

21:33.792 --> 21:36.503
Hey, Director, don't you think
that's inappropriate?

21:36.586 --> 21:39.089
You knew it was inappropriate
to go out with Chae Yu-jin, and yet…

21:39.172 --> 21:40.173
Hey, now, that's…
[sighs]

21:41.675 --> 21:43.468
[chuckles]
Wow.

21:44.803 --> 21:47.306
You're pretty scary now, huh?
I gotta watch out.

21:48.348 --> 21:49.266
So what?

21:49.349 --> 21:52.102
You want to see
how I'd react if I saw him around?

21:52.185 --> 21:54.229
Is that what you wanted, revenge?

21:54.313 --> 21:55.480
What?

21:55.564 --> 21:56.440
[sighs]

21:56.523 --> 21:58.692
I guess you're willing
to do anything to torment me.

21:58.775 --> 22:01.236
You thought I was weak, huh?
Well, I'm not.

22:01.820 --> 22:05.324
I'm not gonna let something small
like this get under my skin, okay?

22:05.407 --> 22:06.241
[sighs]

22:06.325 --> 22:08.368
- Han Ki-jun, stop imagining things--
- Wait a minute.

22:10.329 --> 22:11.246
Are you…

22:13.582 --> 22:15.625
still heartbroken over us?

22:15.709 --> 22:17.794
- [quirky music]
- [sighs]

22:17.878 --> 22:20.172
Hey, Ha-kyung, come on here.

22:20.756 --> 22:22.758
Okay. So you moved him
to Headquarters? What now?

22:23.675 --> 22:25.177
I married her.

22:25.260 --> 22:27.262
You can't make me come back to you--

22:27.346 --> 22:29.389
Ah!
[groans in pain]

22:30.348 --> 22:31.266
[Ha-kyung groans]

22:31.349 --> 22:34.603
I already had enough on my plate
this morning, now this bullshit.

22:34.686 --> 22:37.773
Hey, call me outside like this
one more time, and I'll…

22:37.856 --> 22:40.317
If it happens again,
I'll file a report against you,

22:40.400 --> 22:41.610
and you'll be reprimanded.

22:41.693 --> 22:43.737
- Okay, Deputy Director?
- [groans]

22:45.697 --> 22:48.283
- [quirky music continues]
- [groans]

22:51.411 --> 22:52.788
Yeah, I was right.

22:53.580 --> 22:55.415
[sighs]
Still heartbroken over us.

22:57.042 --> 22:58.126
[groans]

22:59.252 --> 23:01.880
SAFE COUNTRY, PEACEFUL PEOPLE

23:01.963 --> 23:03.632
[phone vibrates]

23:08.011 --> 23:09.221
[Si-woo sighs]

23:12.224 --> 23:14.476
[pensive music]

23:20.732 --> 23:21.733
I pulled all the…

23:21.817 --> 23:24.027
all the flash floods
that caused a lot of damage.

23:24.111 --> 23:25.237
Okay. Put it down.

23:26.196 --> 23:27.197
Over here?

23:29.032 --> 23:30.033
[Si-woo] Uh…

23:32.452 --> 23:34.162
Do you want anything to drink right now?

23:34.913 --> 23:35.747
No, I'm okay.

23:36.748 --> 23:38.208
[mouse clicking]

23:38.291 --> 23:39.876
Listen, are you upset with me?

23:45.132 --> 23:46.133
What are you saying?

23:46.716 --> 23:47.759
It seems like you are.

23:48.343 --> 23:52.013
Is it because I disagreed with you
in front of the Director General?

23:52.722 --> 23:54.224
Did that irritate you?

23:55.225 --> 23:57.102
[sighs]
Listen, Forecaster.

23:58.645 --> 24:00.856
[uneasy music]

24:07.821 --> 24:08.655
Come on.

24:11.074 --> 24:12.701
[footsteps receding]

24:14.828 --> 24:17.080
[uneasy music continues]

24:20.500 --> 24:23.420
[Soo-jin] Why did he have to show off
in front of the Director General?

24:24.379 --> 24:25.922
Now we're all suffering,

24:26.006 --> 24:27.883
- because he made Director Jin angry--
- Stop.

24:27.966 --> 24:30.051
Go analyze if you have time to complain.

24:30.886 --> 24:31.845
Hmm.

24:33.972 --> 24:35.974
[keyboard clacking]

24:36.975 --> 24:37.809
[door slides open]

24:43.440 --> 24:44.524
[door closes]

24:47.110 --> 24:48.695
Forecaster, you--
[gasps]

24:48.778 --> 24:52.199
[tender music]

24:54.993 --> 24:56.036
What are you doing?

24:56.620 --> 24:58.413
Don't worry. We're alone.

24:59.372 --> 25:00.790
Is this why you provoked me?

25:02.000 --> 25:03.168
I didn't know such thing.

25:03.835 --> 25:06.087
I asked because I was really worried.

25:07.714 --> 25:10.842
While we're at work, stay at least
one meter away from me. Clear?

25:10.926 --> 25:12.177
[chuckles]

25:16.932 --> 25:19.434
So, uh, what did you
and Ki-jun talk about?

25:21.561 --> 25:24.397
I just wanted to know why that guy
would have, uh, wanted

25:24.481 --> 25:26.441
to, uh, talk to you outside.

25:27.567 --> 25:28.526
[sighs]

25:29.486 --> 25:31.446
I didn't ask you,
so why are you asking me?

25:33.323 --> 25:35.158
[tender music continues]

25:35.825 --> 25:38.536
I didn't ask you why Chae Yu-jin
was calling you in the morning.

25:38.620 --> 25:39.955
So why would you ask me?

25:40.705 --> 25:41.665
[snickers]

25:42.207 --> 25:44.542
Is that why you were so cold over?

25:45.669 --> 25:46.878
Well, I didn't say that.

25:48.588 --> 25:50.882
- It's true, though, isn't it?
- One meter.

25:52.550 --> 25:54.010
- That was why--
- One meter.

25:56.179 --> 25:59.432
I guess Han Ki-jun found out
I used to go out with her.

25:59.516 --> 26:01.810
It seemed like he was giving Yu-jin
a hard time.

26:01.893 --> 26:05.855
She asked me to be more careful,
so I said I would. That's it.

26:07.482 --> 26:09.943
I understand.
Ki-jun does like to hold a grudge.

26:10.026 --> 26:11.152
[inhales]

26:11.236 --> 26:14.322
And it's your turn to tell me
what Han Ki-jun wanted.

26:15.782 --> 26:17.200
[inhales]

26:17.284 --> 26:22.414
He asked, uh, if I was trying to hurt him
by adding you to my team.

26:22.497 --> 26:26.293
If it was on purpose or what
because you're his wife's ex-boyfriend.

26:26.376 --> 26:28.003
Why would I want revenge?

26:28.086 --> 26:31.089
Also, we wouldn't have started
all this madness

26:31.172 --> 26:32.716
just to get revenge on anyone.

26:32.799 --> 26:33.717
Am I right?

26:33.800 --> 26:36.803
- "Madness"? Really?
- [chuckles]

26:36.886 --> 26:40.348
I just suffered through so much
for dating a coworker, now here we are.

26:40.432 --> 26:42.684
So, yeah. Madness sounds right.

26:42.767 --> 26:45.145
[sweet music]

26:46.438 --> 26:47.856
You make a good point.

26:50.483 --> 26:52.485
[sweet music continues]

26:53.028 --> 26:56.573
I'm just mad I didn't catch
the cold air coming from the north.

26:58.408 --> 26:59.451
Yeah, I know.

27:01.745 --> 27:03.246
Okay, then. See you.

27:04.873 --> 27:06.416
Can I come to your place after work?

27:08.209 --> 27:09.711
If you bring a bottle of Pinot Noir.

27:09.794 --> 27:10.920
Done!

27:11.004 --> 27:12.672
- [door opens]
- [gasps]

27:13.506 --> 27:14.549
[music stops]

27:16.885 --> 27:19.262
Stop messing around. Okay, Forecaster?

27:19.888 --> 27:20.847
Yes, ma'am.

27:22.390 --> 27:23.224
[sighs in relief]

27:25.060 --> 27:27.437
[playful music]

27:29.189 --> 27:30.648
[machine clicks, beeps]

27:30.732 --> 27:31.775
[chuckles]

27:32.442 --> 27:34.194
She's so annoyed with me right now.

27:34.944 --> 27:36.571
She's actually really harsh.

27:37.238 --> 27:38.823
You wouldn't think so, and well…

27:38.907 --> 27:40.992
Mm. Yeah, no one asked.

27:43.370 --> 27:44.579
'Kay.

27:51.419 --> 27:52.712
[glass clinking]

27:57.092 --> 27:58.176
[music stops]

28:02.680 --> 28:04.974
[ice clinking]

28:11.564 --> 28:13.817
We have a washing machine, you know.

28:15.360 --> 28:16.236
[grunts]

28:17.570 --> 28:19.155
Have you heard from Ha-kyung yet?

28:21.074 --> 28:24.536
Mom, these days, people even
wanna have a dog choose its own life.

28:24.619 --> 28:26.996
So it's not at all cool for a mother

28:27.080 --> 28:29.374
to submit all
of her daughter's information

28:29.457 --> 28:32.919
to a matchmaking plan
and not even ever go and ask her.

28:34.421 --> 28:36.005
I didn't do it for me.

28:36.089 --> 28:38.716
If she marries a guy
that's actually worth her time,

28:38.800 --> 28:42.929
her life will be simple, and I'd be
so proud to tell everyone about it.

28:43.847 --> 28:45.724
I sacrificed so much raising her.

28:45.807 --> 28:47.976
So can't I have
this one thing as a parent?

28:48.059 --> 28:50.895
[sighs]
That's more for you than for Ha-kyung.

28:50.979 --> 28:52.313
Ah, shut it.

28:52.397 --> 28:53.690
Go in.
[sighs]

28:53.773 --> 28:56.860
Do some work. Don't leave
your deadline to the last second.

28:58.486 --> 28:59.404
[huffs]

29:02.198 --> 29:04.951
[rustling]

29:09.789 --> 29:11.124
Should I call her?

29:13.042 --> 29:15.920
Just forget it. I'm a woman with pride.

29:18.673 --> 29:21.259
[dramatic music]

29:21.342 --> 29:23.928
- [sighs]
- You can have it, Mom.

29:24.012 --> 29:25.096
[scoffs]

29:26.639 --> 29:28.391
[breathes heavily]

29:30.018 --> 29:32.353
[quirky music]

29:32.437 --> 29:33.354
[music stops]

29:40.779 --> 29:41.988
What's wrong, huh?

29:42.989 --> 29:44.073
Nothing.

29:44.157 --> 29:45.617
Did you have a fight with your husband?

29:46.493 --> 29:47.410
No, we didn't fight.

29:47.994 --> 29:49.496
What's it about? In-laws?

29:49.579 --> 29:51.915
Different lifestyles?
Or does he want to have a child?

29:51.998 --> 29:53.082
Nothing like that.

29:53.792 --> 29:55.668
[approaching footsteps]

29:55.752 --> 29:57.921
Oh, hi. Mind if I join my wife?

29:58.004 --> 30:00.006
[chuckles]
Oh, hello, Deputy Director.

30:00.089 --> 30:01.257
Please eat.

30:03.426 --> 30:05.053
Why, uh, why just soup, huh?

30:05.136 --> 30:06.471
The bulgogi looked good today.

30:08.223 --> 30:09.224
Here, try.

30:09.307 --> 30:10.725
[indistinct chatter]

30:12.227 --> 30:13.520
[Ki-jun grunts]

30:13.603 --> 30:14.479
[Yu-jin chuckles]

30:15.355 --> 30:18.566
[chuckles]
Yu-jin will always go for a great steak.

30:19.150 --> 30:21.194
And she never even ever gains a pound.

30:21.277 --> 30:23.279
Some people just have
really amazing genetics, huh?

30:23.363 --> 30:26.032
Oh, yeah. Right.
[nervous laughter]

30:26.616 --> 30:28.451
[phone vibrates]

30:31.329 --> 30:32.705
Give me a minute, okay?

30:37.252 --> 30:38.378
- [slurps]
- What are you doing?

30:39.754 --> 30:41.631
I'm helping you save your reputation.

30:42.423 --> 30:44.050
Why? Should I not?

30:44.133 --> 30:46.135
Do you want me to show up
and keep arguing instead?

30:46.219 --> 30:47.554
"Arguing"?

30:48.179 --> 30:49.264
You were the one who--

30:49.347 --> 30:50.849
Huh, what were you saying to her?

30:50.932 --> 30:52.725
[quirky music]

30:53.434 --> 30:54.561
Oh, hello.

30:57.897 --> 31:00.275
That jerk was so cocky earlier.

31:00.358 --> 31:02.569
He didn't even seem sorry or guilty.

31:02.652 --> 31:04.529
Why would he be sorry or guilty?

31:04.612 --> 31:05.780
We're not together.

31:06.823 --> 31:09.075
Are you really taking that bastard's side?

31:09.158 --> 31:10.451
It's not like that.

31:10.952 --> 31:13.663
Regardless, I don't even want you
seeing him by accident anymore.

31:13.746 --> 31:16.791
And if you do run into him,
don't even say hi.

31:16.875 --> 31:18.376
Don't look at him, get it?

31:18.459 --> 31:20.587
Well, how about you just ask me to quit?

31:22.213 --> 31:23.464
- Would you?
- Oppa.

31:23.548 --> 31:25.884
There's ton of other places
for a reporter to work,

31:25.967 --> 31:27.886
like police stations
or the Prosecutors' Office.

31:27.969 --> 31:30.555
Why don't you move to another office
if you're so uncomfortable?

31:30.638 --> 31:31.890
Hey, hey.

31:31.973 --> 31:34.559
My job here is perfect.
You know I can't go.

31:35.268 --> 31:36.477
And listen to me, Yu-jin.

31:36.561 --> 31:39.230
You better stop talking back
to me like that.

31:39.814 --> 31:42.275
I'm only letting it slide
because I'm so nice.

31:42.358 --> 31:44.235
[scoffs]
Hard to imagine you if you weren't.

31:44.861 --> 31:48.656
Anyway, I really hope
you won't lie to me ever again, okay?

31:49.240 --> 31:52.452
[Eun-ji] Gosh, I'm sorry.
My family just called.

31:52.535 --> 31:54.287
[chuckles]
Eat your soup. It's getting cold.

31:54.370 --> 31:55.246
[laughs]

31:55.330 --> 31:56.372
You too, babe.

31:58.249 --> 31:59.208
[inhales]

32:02.378 --> 32:06.215
[playful music]

32:08.134 --> 32:09.010
[Ki-jun] Mm.

32:12.305 --> 32:13.264
Eat it all up.

32:14.599 --> 32:16.267
[laughs]
You're making me blush

32:16.351 --> 32:17.644
in front of Reporter Cho.

32:17.727 --> 32:20.271
See? Yu-jin cares about me so much.

32:20.355 --> 32:21.314
[both laugh]

32:21.898 --> 32:22.815
Ooh.

32:24.275 --> 32:25.985
[Ki-jun] Mm, delicious.

32:26.069 --> 32:27.028
Mm.

32:28.655 --> 32:30.657
[playful music]

32:37.330 --> 32:39.749
[playful music continues]

32:40.959 --> 32:43.044
- One Americano, please.
- [barista] Of course.

32:43.962 --> 32:47.840
[woman] I heard Director Jin lost it
because some new guy stood up to her.

32:49.092 --> 32:51.719
Well, it wasn't that bad, though.
[chuckles]

32:51.803 --> 32:53.262
[man] I heard Ms. Kim Soo-jin

32:53.346 --> 32:56.224
from your team complaining
and pouting about it.

32:56.307 --> 32:59.143
She said that
Director General scolded Director Jin

32:59.227 --> 33:02.313
and she got so mad, she made the team
analyze ten years' worth of data.

33:02.397 --> 33:05.692
I just think it's wrong to take it out
on your subordinates like that, you know?

33:05.775 --> 33:07.402
You must be having a hard time.

33:08.361 --> 33:10.405
[woman] It was nice
when Director Choi was around.

33:10.488 --> 33:11.656
[chuckles]
Well…

33:11.739 --> 33:13.783
I'm sure she'll figure things out soon.

33:14.367 --> 33:15.618
[barista] Here's your Americano.

33:16.744 --> 33:19.372
She does scare me a little
every time I see her.

33:19.455 --> 33:21.165
'Cause she seems so cold.

33:21.249 --> 33:23.584
- [man] I know.
- [Myung-ju] It's not fair.

33:25.420 --> 33:28.256
[pensive music]

33:28.339 --> 33:31.134
[papers rustle]

33:42.270 --> 33:43.229
[sighs]

33:51.863 --> 33:55.366
[foreboding music]

33:55.950 --> 33:58.703
[monitor beeping]

33:58.786 --> 34:01.247
[ominous music]

34:03.374 --> 34:04.417
[Si-woo] Director Jin.

34:06.461 --> 34:07.628
Gone to lunch yet?

34:09.881 --> 34:11.591
Oh, I'm coming back from it.

34:11.674 --> 34:13.718
We had kalguksu
at the place up the street.

34:13.801 --> 34:16.054
Mm, sounds good.

34:17.889 --> 34:20.475
Oh, uh, didn't you say you were staying

34:20.558 --> 34:21.851
- at the training center, Si-woo?
- Yeah.

34:21.934 --> 34:24.479
Then how did you run
into Director Jin this morning?

34:26.439 --> 34:28.149
The training center is right over there.

34:28.232 --> 34:31.152
[uneasy music]

34:33.696 --> 34:34.655
Uh…

34:35.656 --> 34:36.866
Uh…
[chuckles]

34:37.742 --> 34:39.869
[phone ringing]

34:41.329 --> 34:43.372
Yes, this is Kim Soo-jin
from Chief Team Two.

34:43.456 --> 34:45.750
[man] I'm calling about the rain echo
in Seoul right now.

34:46.542 --> 34:47.668
E… echo?

34:50.046 --> 34:51.047
Ah, just a moment.

34:52.256 --> 34:54.801
Mr. Um, it's the Metropolitan Office.

34:54.884 --> 34:57.053
They're saying the rain echo
over Seoul looks abnormal.

34:57.136 --> 34:59.055
- Could you please take a look?
- Huh?

34:59.764 --> 35:00.681
What?

35:01.432 --> 35:02.391
Oh!

35:02.475 --> 35:04.685
[foreboding music]

35:04.769 --> 35:08.689
NATIONAL METEOROLOGICAL CENTER
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

35:09.440 --> 35:11.567
What? But why?

35:11.651 --> 35:14.320
[foreboding music rises]

35:14.403 --> 35:17.865
- Tsk, touring a house that early?
- Yeah, an apartment.

35:19.367 --> 35:21.619
I guess the landlord's schedule
was really full,

35:21.702 --> 35:23.621
so they were only available
in the morning, right?

35:23.704 --> 35:24.580
That's, that's right?

35:24.664 --> 35:26.249
Oh, yeah, that's the story.

35:26.332 --> 35:29.293
It was all the landlord's schedule. Yeah.

35:29.377 --> 35:31.462
[nervous chuckle]

35:32.755 --> 35:35.508
You sure know a lot about the tour,
considering you weren't there.

35:35.591 --> 35:37.635
[quirky music]

35:39.554 --> 35:42.098
[chuckles]
I know.

35:43.307 --> 35:44.142
[sighs]

35:44.225 --> 35:45.309
[Ha-kyung chuckles]

35:49.105 --> 35:50.148
[thunder roars]

35:50.231 --> 35:52.400
[rain pattering]

35:53.985 --> 35:56.362
[rain pouring heavily]

35:56.445 --> 35:59.198
[dramatic music]

35:59.282 --> 36:01.659
[loud rain pattering]

36:03.661 --> 36:05.788
[panicked muttering]

36:05.872 --> 36:07.999
[tense music]

36:11.502 --> 36:14.338
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

36:15.590 --> 36:16.841
[woman] Let's hurry home.

36:17.592 --> 36:19.093
[kid] Mom, I'm getting wet!

36:20.094 --> 36:22.305
[tense music continues]

36:23.890 --> 36:24.974
It's raining.

36:27.810 --> 36:28.936
What should we do?

36:29.020 --> 36:31.022
[rain pattering]

36:35.026 --> 36:37.862
Let's go!
[both screaming]

36:37.945 --> 36:39.447
Come on! Hurry!

36:44.118 --> 36:46.204
[tense music]

36:51.709 --> 36:52.627
[grunts]

36:52.710 --> 36:55.046
[Tae-kyung] Mom, did the weather forecast
say that it would rain?

36:55.129 --> 36:56.130
Oh, no!

36:56.214 --> 36:57.798
- [Mrs. Bae] Goodness!
- [Tae-kyung shrieks]

36:57.882 --> 36:59.300
[Mrs. Bae] They didn't say anything.

37:00.676 --> 37:02.929
Do you think I would
have hung the laundry out for this?

37:03.012 --> 37:04.347
- Oh.
- [groans]

37:05.681 --> 37:07.099
- Gosh. Darn it.
- Oh, no.

37:08.059 --> 37:10.019
It's like all hell's breaking loose.

37:11.229 --> 37:13.814
[rain pattering]

37:16.359 --> 37:19.320
Hey, KMA! What do you guys
even do over there, huh?

37:19.403 --> 37:21.739
Why didn't you say anything
about this sudden rainstorm?

37:21.822 --> 37:25.117
This is why they say you guys
are never right about anything! Jesus!

37:27.036 --> 37:27.912
[grumbles]

37:27.995 --> 37:29.455
[water dripping]

37:29.538 --> 37:32.833
AUTOMATIC CONTROL PANEL

37:35.211 --> 37:38.047
[water dripping heavily]

37:42.760 --> 37:44.387
[fire crackles]

37:44.470 --> 37:46.097
[flickering, buzzing]

37:47.098 --> 37:48.140
- Huh?
- [lights clicking]

37:48.224 --> 37:49.809
- [man 1] What's going on?
- [woman 1] The lights are out.

37:49.892 --> 37:52.853
- [man 2] Oh, my God.
- [woman 2] Huh? What's happening?

37:53.521 --> 37:55.273
Is it our problem or the city?

37:55.356 --> 37:58.276
- [man 2] We should go check the fuse.
- [woman 1] Hey, get some more…

37:58.359 --> 38:01.487
I don't care! The entire building
has no power right now!

38:01.570 --> 38:04.365
What are you going to do? You know
how much this is gonna cost us, huh?

38:04.907 --> 38:07.618
I think you should find a new line of work
if you can't even forecast rain.

38:07.702 --> 38:08.786
You're wasting all our won.

38:08.869 --> 38:11.789
Are you going to compensate us for all
the business we're losing right now?

38:14.292 --> 38:15.918
Why weren't you monitoring the live data?

38:16.961 --> 38:18.170
I was.

38:18.254 --> 38:19.422
And then…

38:21.465 --> 38:22.508
I missed it.

38:24.719 --> 38:26.345
Why? What were you doing?

38:29.223 --> 38:32.101
Is there something up with you?
Are you doing this purposely?

38:32.184 --> 38:34.353
Director, I think
that's too much, you know.

38:34.437 --> 38:37.648
A forecaster ignoring live data
is dereliction of duties.

38:37.732 --> 38:40.693
If the damage is severe enough,
you could be let go from your station.

38:40.776 --> 38:41.819
[Seok-ho sighs]

38:42.486 --> 38:44.322
Even if we saw the rain echo,

38:44.405 --> 38:47.074
there only would have been
a few minutes before it started.

38:47.158 --> 38:48.659
The flooding couldn't have been
prevented regardless.

38:48.743 --> 38:50.328
The damage would have been less serious.

38:50.411 --> 38:52.496
How? It'd still rain 80mm per hour.

38:52.580 --> 38:53.789
[Dong-han] That's enough.

38:53.873 --> 38:55.041
I'm sorry.

38:55.124 --> 38:56.917
It's my fault, okay? Stop it.

39:00.087 --> 39:01.005
[sighs]

39:02.381 --> 39:03.466
I'm sorry.

39:04.675 --> 39:07.595
I missed the rainstorm
'cause I was going through old reports.

39:09.513 --> 39:10.890
So what are you saying?

39:13.392 --> 39:18.522
Truthfully, isn't it impossible to analyze
ten years of data in one afternoon?

39:19.106 --> 39:21.400
If I had been more focused
on real-time monitoring--

39:21.484 --> 39:23.527
You're very confused, Ms. Kim Soo-jin.

39:25.696 --> 39:30.034
Analysis and real-time reports
are equally important duties here.

39:30.117 --> 39:32.453
Claiming you missed one
because of the other

39:32.536 --> 39:35.039
is lazy and a poor excuse. Got it?

39:35.122 --> 39:37.208
[dramatic music]

39:39.043 --> 39:41.003
But it's not an excuse.

39:42.755 --> 39:44.632
I really tried my best, you know, just--

39:45.841 --> 39:46.926
Um, Ms. Kim…

39:47.009 --> 39:50.304
I'm sorry. I'm sorry
I'm not capable enough for you.

39:51.764 --> 39:56.435
Still, I was trying hard, okay?
So please stop implying that I wasn't.

39:56.519 --> 39:57.561
[sniffles]

39:58.396 --> 40:00.481
[dramatic music continues]

40:01.357 --> 40:02.441
[sighs]

40:03.859 --> 40:05.653
What a great department we are.

40:10.950 --> 40:12.701
[footsteps receding]

40:13.744 --> 40:14.703
[sighs]

40:17.081 --> 40:19.291
[dramatic music]

40:20.793 --> 40:22.711
Director Jin and Senior Forecaster Um.

40:23.421 --> 40:25.172
The Director General wants to see you.

40:26.090 --> 40:27.091
Okay.

40:28.759 --> 40:30.761
[gloomy music]

40:33.097 --> 40:35.683
"As the stream swelled,
the roads were flooded,

40:35.766 --> 40:38.018
12 houses were submerged in water,

40:38.102 --> 40:41.105
and electricity was lost
in an underground mall in Gangnam.

40:41.689 --> 40:44.358
We'll have to wait and see
the full extent of the damage."

40:45.901 --> 40:46.777
Casualties?

40:48.070 --> 40:48.946
[Park] Well…

40:50.072 --> 40:50.990
Are there any?

40:51.073 --> 40:54.160
Two workers went missing
during a routine inspection

40:55.619 --> 40:58.080
of a drainage plant at Anreung.

40:58.831 --> 40:59.915
[Dong-han sighs]

41:01.417 --> 41:03.252
And is the rescue search ongoing?

41:03.335 --> 41:06.672
Emergency services
and facility management have started.

41:07.673 --> 41:09.717
But they haven't reported
any findings yet.

41:09.800 --> 41:11.135
This is a nightmare.

41:12.428 --> 41:13.512
I'm sorry, sir.

41:14.889 --> 41:16.056
It was me.

41:17.099 --> 41:18.142
I missed the signal.

41:19.059 --> 41:22.188
I'll take full responsibility.

41:23.898 --> 41:26.609
[tense music]

41:29.528 --> 41:30.529
[doorknob clicks]

41:34.408 --> 41:36.660
Why are you doing
this whole brooding song and dance?

41:36.744 --> 41:37.578
What?

41:37.661 --> 41:40.206
In front of our department
and now in front of our Director.

41:40.289 --> 41:42.708
Why are you so set
on claiming responsibility?

41:42.791 --> 41:45.127
'Cause I didn't notice the signals.

41:45.211 --> 41:47.171
But why? Why would you, though?

41:47.254 --> 41:49.173
You're supposed to be
the great Um Dong-han.

41:49.256 --> 41:52.051
I heard you could spot a rainstorm
from the scent of the east wind.

41:52.134 --> 41:54.803
My impression is you wouldn't notice
if it rained in here.

41:55.971 --> 41:57.139
[sighs deeply]

41:59.058 --> 41:59.892
What?

42:00.684 --> 42:02.937
Does it bother you that
I'm your superior when I'm newer?

42:03.020 --> 42:05.564
No. It's nothing like that.
I already told you--

42:05.648 --> 42:06.690
Just wait!

42:07.358 --> 42:09.443
Since I'm the director of Team Two,

42:09.527 --> 42:12.154
I'm the one who takes responsibility
for this crisis,

42:12.238 --> 42:14.573
and I don't want you saying
that it will be you.

42:16.033 --> 42:17.159
You're out of line here.

42:23.499 --> 42:24.875
[footsteps receding]

42:27.336 --> 42:28.379
[sighs]

42:29.964 --> 42:31.090
[grumbles]

42:31.924 --> 42:34.343
[pensive music]

42:36.303 --> 42:37.179
[sighs]

42:37.263 --> 42:39.807
[Si-woo] People think weather
and climate are the same,

42:39.890 --> 42:41.308
but they are quite different.

42:42.268 --> 42:44.520
- [documents clatter]
- [gasps, sighs]

42:46.063 --> 42:49.024
[Si-woo] While weather changes
from day to day like your feelings,

42:49.108 --> 42:53.362
climate stays consistent through time,
like someone's innate personality.

42:56.323 --> 42:58.784
How can you adapt
to someone's feelings in the moment

42:58.867 --> 43:00.869
when you don't know their personality?

43:01.954 --> 43:03.956
[pensive music continues]

43:05.374 --> 43:06.292
[sniffles]

43:06.375 --> 43:08.460
[Soo-jin] Are you taking
Director Jin's side?

43:08.544 --> 43:09.670
Ah, no.

43:10.379 --> 43:12.339
I'm here to tell you I was wrong.

43:14.466 --> 43:18.053
While I was just trying
to predict the weather, well, see,

43:18.137 --> 43:20.764
Director Jin tried to analyze in detail

43:20.848 --> 43:25.811
how the infinite systems of climate
would actually affect everybody.

43:25.894 --> 43:28.439
Even if the same amount of rain
falls at the same time,

43:28.522 --> 43:31.233
the impact varies from region to region.

43:32.651 --> 43:36.864
When it rains 80mm per hour everywhere,
Yeoksam will be just fine,

43:36.947 --> 43:40.868
but Gangnam will be flooded
because, well, the ground there is lower.

43:42.620 --> 43:46.040
A forecast should reflect that as well.

43:46.123 --> 43:50.252
So it's important to analyze
all the data we can at all times.

43:50.336 --> 43:51.211
[inhales]

43:53.464 --> 43:54.715
[inhales sharply]

43:54.798 --> 43:57.760
She asked us to analyze
ten years' worth of data

43:57.843 --> 43:59.803
to make consumer-centered forecasts,

44:00.846 --> 44:03.682
not forecasts just for…
for the scientists.

44:03.766 --> 44:06.435
I was too focused
on performance and results.

44:07.102 --> 44:10.564
But Director Jin was thinking
of what the people actually need,

44:11.649 --> 44:12.858
what really counts.

44:14.860 --> 44:15.986
[sniffles]

44:17.071 --> 44:19.448
Well, it's really hard.

44:21.116 --> 44:22.076
I know.

44:23.827 --> 44:24.787
[inhales]

44:26.163 --> 44:27.164
[exhales deeply]

44:27.748 --> 44:29.833
[pensive music]

44:32.127 --> 44:33.128
[Myung-ju sighs]

44:34.630 --> 44:35.798
[music fades]

44:37.591 --> 44:39.510
How are you feeling
about your team members?

44:40.344 --> 44:41.345
Sorry?

44:42.721 --> 44:45.391
Taking responsibility is important.

44:45.474 --> 44:49.019
But you aren't the only one
who's been working hard.

44:49.520 --> 44:52.231
We're all professionals,
and we're all trying to do right.

44:54.942 --> 44:57.027
All of us take this seriously.

44:57.111 --> 44:59.029
[rustling]

45:00.739 --> 45:04.201
You trust that we'll do our best
on the work that you assign us, don't you?

45:04.284 --> 45:07.371
Honestly, I don't think our team
has much confidence in me right now.

45:08.163 --> 45:10.541
They don't have faith
in my orders or decisions.

45:10.624 --> 45:11.917
[chuckles, tongue clicks]

45:12.418 --> 45:14.753
It's not your orders
that we don't have faith in.

45:15.421 --> 45:16.422
We don't have faith in you

45:16.505 --> 45:20.926
because you're obviously unsure
about your own orders.

45:24.513 --> 45:25.389
Hmm. Ah!

45:26.557 --> 45:27.599
Here.

45:27.683 --> 45:31.437
I analyzed data related to localized
flash floods over the past ten years.

45:31.937 --> 45:33.939
In addition to the main causes
of heavy showers,

45:34.022 --> 45:37.401
I also included cases related
to convergence and divergence

45:37.484 --> 45:39.027
of upper and lower jet streams.

45:39.111 --> 45:39.987
It's all there.

45:40.737 --> 45:41.822
[chuckles]

45:41.905 --> 45:42.948
Uh…

45:43.699 --> 45:46.368
Well, I finished what you wanted,
so I guess I'll head out.

45:46.452 --> 45:48.912
[chuckles]
Shouldn't you head out too?

45:48.996 --> 45:50.998
- [soft chuckle]
- [phone vibrates]

45:53.208 --> 45:54.793
Ah, Mom.

45:54.877 --> 45:56.670
Did the kids get soaked earlier?

45:57.504 --> 45:59.798
[giggles]
I know, right?

45:59.882 --> 46:00.799
[inhales]

46:02.718 --> 46:04.178
Exactly. Oh, yes.

46:04.970 --> 46:07.639
I work at the KMA,
and my kids still get caught in it.

46:08.265 --> 46:09.266
[Myung-ju laughs]

46:11.226 --> 46:12.436
[elevator dings]

46:13.896 --> 46:14.897
[elevator door closes]

46:24.740 --> 46:25.699
[phone beeps]

46:31.705 --> 46:33.373
[Ki-jun] Hey, Yu-jin. It's oppa.

46:34.208 --> 46:36.877
I'm heading out right now. Wait for me.

46:37.377 --> 46:40.088
So what do you feel like
for dinner tonight, huh, doll?

46:40.672 --> 46:42.716
Oh, tteokbokki.

46:43.217 --> 46:45.886
Sure. I'll get anything for you, my baby.

46:46.762 --> 46:47.846
[snickers]

46:48.805 --> 46:50.182
[whispers]
No. No, no, no.

46:51.433 --> 46:53.644
[playful music]

46:55.312 --> 46:56.313
[chuckles]

46:57.814 --> 46:58.982
[elevator dings]

46:59.900 --> 47:01.276
- Okay. See you.
- [man] Goodbye.

47:03.612 --> 47:06.490
- Oh, uh, you're going home now?
- [Seok-ho] Yeah. You?

47:06.573 --> 47:07.407
I should.

47:07.991 --> 47:09.952
Everyone left already. I'm the last one.

47:19.461 --> 47:24.174
ANREUNG RAINWATER DRAINAGE STATION

47:24.258 --> 47:25.968
EMERGENCY RESCUE CONTROL
ON-SITE COMMAND

47:26.051 --> 47:28.470
[sirens wailing]

47:29.513 --> 47:31.181
THIRD PRESS BRIEFING

47:31.265 --> 47:33.850
ANREUNG DRAINAGE STATION
SEARCH FOR MISSING PEOPLE

47:33.934 --> 47:35.477
MISSING WORKERS: 2 PEOPLE

47:35.561 --> 47:39.189
- [indistinct chatter]
- [pensive music]

47:43.986 --> 47:45.988
[machine humming]

47:48.991 --> 47:50.325
[sirens wailing]

47:51.243 --> 47:53.453
[rescuer 1]
Do you see anything? Keep looking.

47:53.537 --> 47:54.705
[rescuer 2] Shine the light here.

47:54.788 --> 47:56.039
[rescuer 1] Look over there too.

47:56.123 --> 47:56.999
- Okay.
- Over there.

47:57.082 --> 47:58.375
[rescuer 3] Our time is running out.

47:58.458 --> 48:00.419
[rescuer 1] We have to check
over there too.

48:01.670 --> 48:03.213
I think they're maybe down there.

48:03.297 --> 48:04.923
[rescuer 2] Shine the light over there.

48:09.094 --> 48:11.805
[sirens wailing]

48:11.888 --> 48:14.016
[pensive music continues]

48:26.445 --> 48:28.405
DANGER

48:28.488 --> 48:29.615
Why are you here?

48:30.616 --> 48:31.450
Oh.

48:32.034 --> 48:34.077
I couldn't sleep, so I thought I should…

48:35.120 --> 48:36.496
I should at least show up,

48:36.580 --> 48:39.791
so they don't think
I'm completely heartless.

48:41.001 --> 48:43.170
- The workers?
- Not yet.

48:46.006 --> 48:46.882
[sniffles]

48:46.965 --> 48:48.842
[siren wailing]

48:50.010 --> 48:51.887
[jacket rustles]

48:55.015 --> 48:56.224
Thank you.

49:01.980 --> 49:05.025
[phone vibrating]

49:10.155 --> 49:11.740
[line ringing]

49:11.823 --> 49:13.867
[soft music playing]

49:15.410 --> 49:16.662
Oh!
[chuckles]

49:16.745 --> 49:19.790
[operator] The person you are trying
to reach is not available at this time.

49:20.415 --> 49:21.750
Oh, okay, then.

49:22.793 --> 49:23.919
[sucks teeth]

49:24.544 --> 49:26.546
What would she want, huh?

49:28.632 --> 49:29.716
[sucks teeth]

49:30.634 --> 49:32.678
[phone vibrates]

49:35.389 --> 49:37.808
[foreboding music]

49:50.278 --> 49:52.364
[foreboding music continues]

49:59.913 --> 50:02.749
[tense music]

50:04.084 --> 50:07.045
[siren wailing]

50:07.129 --> 50:09.589
RESTRICTED
KEEP OUT

50:10.882 --> 50:13.093
[rescuer 1] We found them! Over there!

50:13.176 --> 50:15.721
[rescuer 2] They're alive! They're fine!
They're over here!

50:15.804 --> 50:17.389
[glorious music]

50:17.472 --> 50:19.266
[rescuer 3] Please let it down carefully.

50:20.016 --> 50:22.394
- Are you okay, sir? Are you okay?
- [rescuer 4] Clear! Clear!

50:22.477 --> 50:24.438
- Pull the lines. Bring them up.
- Are you okay?

50:26.148 --> 50:28.692
[rescuer 5] Right there,
right there, be careful, huh.

50:29.526 --> 50:32.112
- [rescuer 6] Guys, let's bring him in.
- Oh, thank God.

50:32.195 --> 50:34.531
[sighs]
They're okay.

50:35.699 --> 50:37.701
[rescuer 6] Medic! Get the medic.

50:38.535 --> 50:42.080
- Have you had dinner?
- No. Have you?

50:43.206 --> 50:45.125
Let's go somewhere with a good soup.

50:47.169 --> 50:48.962
[rescuer 7] Bring them over here!
Over here!

50:50.464 --> 50:52.841
Give us some space. Give us some space.

50:57.137 --> 50:58.346
[music fades]

51:04.227 --> 51:05.061
[Ha-kyung] Oh!

51:06.188 --> 51:07.439
You're not staying at home?

51:11.109 --> 51:12.444
Oh, yeah.

51:13.403 --> 51:14.362
It's a long story.

51:19.451 --> 51:20.452
[exhales sharply]

51:22.746 --> 51:24.748
- [elevator dings]
- [automated voice] Door is opening.

51:28.168 --> 51:30.170
Oh, hold on a second.
[panting]

51:30.253 --> 51:31.379
[Tae-kyung] Thank you.

51:33.173 --> 51:35.675
- Which floor?
- Oh, 12th.

51:36.760 --> 51:38.094
[automated voice] Door is closing.

51:40.680 --> 51:42.015
[breathing deeply]

51:50.398 --> 51:52.150
You live right over us.

51:52.234 --> 51:54.986
1302 or is it 1301?
[chuckles]

51:56.196 --> 51:57.572
It's 1302.

51:58.156 --> 51:59.032
Ah.

52:02.369 --> 52:04.788
Well, then, we're neighbors, aren't we?

52:05.288 --> 52:07.332
My sister lives in 1201.

52:08.750 --> 52:10.085
[elevator dings]

52:10.168 --> 52:12.587
[automated voice] Twelfth floor.
Door is opening.

52:12.671 --> 52:14.005
Have a good night.
[soft chuckle]

52:17.634 --> 52:19.010
[automated voice] Door is closing.

52:22.264 --> 52:23.098
[sighs]

52:24.975 --> 52:27.018
[beeping]

52:27.102 --> 52:28.687
Hmm? Hmm.

52:30.522 --> 52:33.316
[keypad beeping]

52:33.400 --> 52:34.734
[doorknob clanks]

52:37.112 --> 52:38.321
[blows air]

52:40.323 --> 52:41.658
[keypad beeping]

52:41.741 --> 52:42.909
Oh, what?

52:43.451 --> 52:44.452
Oh, no.

52:47.163 --> 52:48.039
[sighs]

52:48.123 --> 52:52.085
[classical music playing]

53:03.013 --> 53:04.347
[breathes deeply]

53:11.980 --> 53:13.899
[inhales deeply]

53:21.364 --> 53:22.407
[gulps]

53:23.325 --> 53:24.784
[relieved sigh]

53:27.579 --> 53:29.831
[doorbell rings]

53:29.915 --> 53:30.957
[sighs]

53:32.959 --> 53:34.169
[groans]

53:35.170 --> 53:36.713
[doorbell rings]

53:38.006 --> 53:39.883
What is it now?
[groans]

53:43.803 --> 53:44.804
Uh…

53:47.223 --> 53:48.099
[sighs]

53:49.142 --> 53:50.894
[door lock beeps]

53:52.187 --> 53:53.355
[Tae-kyung chuckles shyly]

53:53.939 --> 53:55.357
Oh, hello again.

53:55.440 --> 53:57.025
Uh, what can I do for you?

53:57.108 --> 54:00.820
I mentioned earlier
that my sister lives downstairs.

54:00.904 --> 54:02.155
And so?

54:02.238 --> 54:04.074
[chuckles]
Well…

54:04.824 --> 54:07.994
- [Tae-kyung] Take these, then?
- What… what for?

54:08.078 --> 54:10.163
Could you please hold on to these
until she comes home?

54:10.246 --> 54:13.416
It's just she's not picking up her phone,
and her door code's changed.

54:13.500 --> 54:15.377
Uh…

54:15.961 --> 54:17.462
Oh, you could ask security.

54:18.213 --> 54:19.255
Oh, I know.

54:19.339 --> 54:22.258
I've already been to their office,
but they're on patrol.

54:22.342 --> 54:23.301
[Tae-kyung sighs]

54:23.843 --> 54:28.390
This is all fresh kimchi and bulgogi
our dear mother made for her daughter.

54:29.182 --> 54:31.101
I wouldn't want it all to go bad.

54:31.184 --> 54:33.561
And I can't just carry it all back home.

54:33.645 --> 54:34.604
[nervous chuckle]

54:36.106 --> 54:38.024
Please just do me a favor.

54:38.108 --> 54:40.110
[quirky music]

54:40.193 --> 54:41.319
Friendly neighbor.

54:41.403 --> 54:43.613
Uh…
[sighs]

54:43.697 --> 54:44.906
[Tae-kyung chuckles]

54:47.742 --> 54:50.495
I told you. You can wait
for your husband and leave together.

54:50.578 --> 54:52.580
He's having dinner at work,
so he'll be late.

54:52.664 --> 54:55.041
- Is that so?
- Thank you so much for your help today.

54:55.125 --> 54:56.501
Of course. It's my pleasure.

54:56.584 --> 54:58.461
- Good night.
- Good night, Grandma.

54:58.545 --> 54:59.838
Oh. All right.

54:59.921 --> 55:01.673
- Good boy. Let's go now.
- My baby.

55:01.756 --> 55:03.049
- Good night.
- Goodbye.

55:03.133 --> 55:06.136
- Let's go.
- I'm not far if you need something.

55:06.219 --> 55:09.264
- Yeah.
- Okay, get home safely.

55:09.889 --> 55:11.307
Oh, you're so tired.

55:11.391 --> 55:13.101
[crickets chirping]

55:13.184 --> 55:14.519
Oh, Papa!

55:15.854 --> 55:16.730
[Myung-ju] Huh?

55:17.397 --> 55:19.190
So why are you here, honey?

55:19.274 --> 55:21.192
You were having dinner with friends.

55:22.193 --> 55:23.862
[sighs]
I didn't go.

55:24.904 --> 55:25.822
Why not?

55:27.866 --> 55:29.909
I had a lot of stuff
I wanted to think about.

55:32.120 --> 55:33.621
[Myung-ju] What's bothering you?

55:35.373 --> 55:36.541
What are you thinking?

55:38.710 --> 55:39.627
Honey.

55:41.171 --> 55:44.632
I wanna take the Level Five
technical exam again.

55:45.425 --> 55:46.342
Hmm?

55:47.802 --> 55:49.679
What will you do about your job?

55:49.763 --> 55:52.098
[pensive music]

55:52.182 --> 55:53.349
[sighs]

55:53.433 --> 55:55.477
I'm considering taking a year off.

55:55.560 --> 55:56.686
What do you think?

55:59.939 --> 56:01.858
[sighs]
Hmm.

56:03.276 --> 56:04.986
Ah, no way. No.

56:05.070 --> 56:05.945
[utensil clanks]

56:06.029 --> 56:09.407
Some people may say
that it's okay to make a mistake,

56:09.491 --> 56:12.619
but in our profession,
we cannot tolerate an error.

56:12.702 --> 56:13.703
You're, you're right.

56:14.496 --> 56:16.998
But we shouldn't have
to take total responsibility either.

56:18.124 --> 56:21.628
Predicting and forecasting,
that's our job.

56:21.711 --> 56:25.882
And all the uncertainty
that goes with it, that's also our job.

56:26.841 --> 56:31.221
But assuming responsibility
for every bad thing that happens at all?

56:31.304 --> 56:33.264
It's absurdity.

56:34.641 --> 56:37.894
You were the one who took
responsibility in the first place.

56:37.977 --> 56:40.396
That's 'cause I slipped up, okay?

56:40.480 --> 56:43.566
I'll be responsible
for the mistake I made.

56:43.650 --> 56:45.610
Always.
[sucks teeth]

56:46.194 --> 56:49.489
One little mistake of ours
can kill someone

56:49.572 --> 56:52.492
or cause them to lose
their life savings entirely.

56:52.575 --> 56:56.871
Always stay hyper vigilant
and look for patterns in the weather.

56:57.539 --> 56:59.666
- Know who said that?
- I don't.

56:59.749 --> 57:00.834
Who was it?

57:02.460 --> 57:03.711
Remember what you told me?

57:03.795 --> 57:07.715
You said when you would train
Level Five officers,

57:08.216 --> 57:12.011
"The systems that safeguard whole nations
depend on weather forecasting.

57:12.887 --> 57:15.598
Therefore, a sense of duty
and responsibility

57:15.682 --> 57:17.725
is everything for a forecaster."

57:18.393 --> 57:19.561
[Ha-kyung scoffs]

57:19.644 --> 57:23.481
If I hadn't taken that class,
I wouldn't be suffering like this now.

57:23.565 --> 57:25.692
I would have been headed straight
to the top, you know.

57:25.775 --> 57:27.986
[laughs]

57:29.362 --> 57:31.239
Did I tell you
to believe in all of that crap?

57:31.823 --> 57:34.909
- That was your choice.
- [scoffs]

57:34.993 --> 57:37.120
[gentle music]

57:41.291 --> 57:42.834
[sighs deeply]

57:42.917 --> 57:45.837
[chuckles]
So what happened to the man I knew then?

57:46.963 --> 57:48.548
What's gotten into you?

57:49.257 --> 57:50.884
[Dong-han sucks teeth]

57:50.967 --> 57:53.094
Well, you know.

57:54.929 --> 57:57.015
I think…
[sucks teeth]

57:57.891 --> 58:00.351
I lost some kind of, of drive and…

58:01.019 --> 58:02.020
Hmm?

58:02.687 --> 58:06.024
What's the real reason? What's it all for?

58:06.691 --> 58:10.111
For who really?
A guy needs to answer that.

58:10.778 --> 58:12.614
[Dong-han sucks teeth]

58:13.948 --> 58:17.327
And now, I don't know how, so, yeah.

58:19.078 --> 58:21.289
[gentle music continues]

58:23.333 --> 58:25.168
[sighs heavily]

58:26.544 --> 58:28.463
[pensive music]

58:32.759 --> 58:33.635
[music fades]

58:40.975 --> 58:43.978
[automated voice] Please wait.
Your transaction has been processed.

58:44.062 --> 58:47.482
[machine beeping, rattling]

58:47.565 --> 58:49.651
[pensive music]

58:50.818 --> 58:52.946
- Please accept your bills.
- [money dispenser opens]

58:53.029 --> 58:54.364
Thank you very much.

58:57.909 --> 59:01.538
Thank you for using our services.
Please make sure you do not leave…

59:01.621 --> 59:03.873
IMI MOTEL

59:09.462 --> 59:13.132
[pensive music continues]

59:21.808 --> 59:23.351
[Ha-kyung] Oh, careful, careful.

59:24.018 --> 59:26.020
- Oh, easy, easy. You're good.
- Oh.

59:26.104 --> 59:29.816
- Okay. Wait a second, Senior Forecaster.
- Yeah.

59:29.899 --> 59:31.734
Where do you live? What's your address?

59:31.818 --> 59:35.697
Gangwon Province,
Gangneung, Science Complex…

59:35.780 --> 59:38.199
Ah, no, not the Gangwon Office.
Your home in Seoul.

59:38.283 --> 59:41.119
- I'll call a ride for you.
- Huh? "Home"?

59:43.288 --> 59:45.123
Oh, home…

59:46.624 --> 59:48.418
I have no home anymore.

59:49.043 --> 59:53.298
Gang… Gangwon, the KMA… It's the KMA.

59:53.381 --> 59:56.134
I have to go to the KMA.

59:57.760 --> 59:58.886
KMA…

01:00:03.808 --> 01:00:06.644
[uneasy music]

01:00:19.949 --> 01:00:22.035
[uneasy music continues]

01:00:24.996 --> 01:00:26.247
[door opens]

01:00:31.044 --> 01:00:32.170
Mr. Lee?

01:00:35.423 --> 01:00:36.591
[Dong-han grumbles]

01:00:36.674 --> 01:00:38.968
Watch the stairs. Oh.

01:00:44.766 --> 01:00:47.935
[tense music]

01:00:50.897 --> 01:00:52.982
[Ha-kyung] We have
different personalities,

01:00:53.566 --> 01:00:54.901
different principles,

01:00:55.401 --> 01:00:57.278
and different wounds.

01:00:58.071 --> 01:01:02.575
So it's only natural
for the atmosphere to become unstable

01:01:02.659 --> 01:01:06.371
and an abnormal climate
to appear when we meet.

01:01:06.454 --> 01:01:08.289
Why are you, uh…

01:01:08.790 --> 01:01:10.625
Why are you, uh…

01:01:11.501 --> 01:01:12.752
You're here.

01:01:13.795 --> 01:01:15.755
[tense music]

01:01:18.424 --> 01:01:25.431
NATIONAL METEOROLOGICAL CENTER
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

01:01:26.265 --> 01:01:29.102
[thunder rumbles]

01:01:29.185 --> 01:01:32.689
IMI MOTEL

01:01:32.772 --> 01:01:34.607
[rain pouring]

01:01:39.946 --> 01:01:42.657
[somber music]

01:01:44.826 --> 01:01:47.662
["Promise You" by Kyuhyun playing]

01:02:11.519 --> 01:02:13.438
[Si-woo] I picked up your phone
'cause your sister called.

01:02:13.521 --> 01:02:15.565
She says your mom is really sick.

01:02:15.648 --> 01:02:17.150
They're taking her to the ER right now.

01:02:17.942 --> 01:02:20.486
She'd never listen to the
Assistant Director saying she should.

01:02:20.570 --> 01:02:22.280
I'm all right. Go on back to work.

01:02:24.323 --> 01:02:26.617
[Myung-han] I say that
it's time for your investment.

01:02:26.701 --> 01:02:28.619
If you really like my boy…

01:02:28.703 --> 01:02:31.581
- Dad, did you say you met with her?
- [gasps]

01:02:31.664 --> 01:02:34.041
[Ha-kyung] All last night,
I couldn't stop thinking…

01:02:36.043 --> 01:02:36.919
[sighs]

01:02:37.003 --> 01:02:38.337
We should reconsider what we're doing.

01:02:39.088 --> 01:02:40.298
You and me.

01:02:41.299 --> 01:02:45.553
["Promise You" by Kyuhyun playing]
